   "text": "I read the structure in three parts and then joined them.\n\n**Macrocycle**\n- The left benzene carries a CN group. Its two ortho-related ring carbons bear a CH2\u2013O\u2013 link and a propyl chain, \u2013CH2CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013.\n- The propyl chain ends on the O of the middle phenyl ring. That O-bearing carbon is adjacent to the carbon carrying the CH2C(=O) side chain.\n- The pyridyl group is meta to that O on the middle ring. The pyridine nitrogen sits between the carbon bonded to the phenyl and the carbon bonded to the O\u2013CH2 link, which closes the macrocycle.\n\n**Central benzene (amide side)**\n- The amide N\u2013H sits on the ring carbon between the NH\u2013CH2-oxetane carbon and the O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013N(Boc)(CH2CF3) carbon.\n- A methyl ester is on the carbon meta to the amide N.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The only stereo marker is the hashed bond from the CH2 to the oxetane C2.\n- I took the narrow end of the hash to be at the oxetane carbon, so the CH2N group points away from the viewer and the implicit H points toward the viewer.\n- The CIP priorities are O > CH2N > ring CH2 > H, and the drawing gives S.\n- In the SMILES, `NC[C@@H]2CCO2` encodes S, so I used `@@`.\n\nSMILES: N#Cc1ccc2c(c1)CCCOc1cc(ccc1CC(=O)Nc1c(NC[C@@H]3CCO3)cc(C(=O)OC)cc1OCCN(CC(F)(F)F)C(=O)OC(C)(C)C)-c1cccc(n1)OC2"
